-- A host's thing held by a `with`, the same for every effect: an open
-- file, a socket, a canvas.  `scoped acquire release body` acquires it,
-- runs `body` with it, a `With s r` in a region `s` of its own, and
-- releases it when `body` ends.  The body is polymorphic in `s`, and
-- what it comes to is of a type bound outside it, so a `With s r`
-- cannot leave the body (as Haskell's `ST`): a `with` of one effect may
-- hand its thing to an operation of another by value -- a canvas found
-- by the DOM, drawn on by the GPU -- and neither keeps it.
--
-- `With` is exposed without its tag: no program makes one, and `scoped`
-- is the only `with`.  A library wraps `scoped` around its own
-- operations acquiring and releasing the thing, exposes that `withX`
-- alone -- never the bare acquire, as a bare host value given `scoped`
-- is a use after its close -- and gives the thing to a provider
-- operation by `inside`, which takes it out for that operation and
-- nothing else: a program has no use for it, as the operations take the
-- `With`.
--
-- The thing is the host's own, a foreign value with a finalizer, so a
-- body left otherwise -- a throw heard outside it, a handler between
-- that drops the continuation -- lets go of it where the program drops
-- its last reference to it; `scoped` adds nothing for that.

module (With, scoped, inside)

import co

-- | A host's thing, held in the region `s` by a `with` (`scoped`).
data With (s : Type) a = MkWith a

-- | The thing a `with` holds, for a provider operation given it: a
-- | library's operation on a `With s a` takes it out here and gives it
-- | to the operation, and nothing else does.
inside : {s : Type} -> {a : Type} -> With s a -> a
inside (MkWith x) = x

-- (what the body came to, or why the thing was not released)
closedWith : {err a : Type} -> a -> Either err Unit -> Either err a
closedWith x (Right _) = Right x
closedWith x (Left err) = Left err

-- (the body run with the thing, then the thing released; or why it was
-- not acquired)
heldBy : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {err r a : Type}
       -> (r -> Co e (Either err Unit))
       -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
       -> Either err r
       -> Co e (Either err a)
heldBy release body (Left err) = pure (Left err)
heldBy release body (Right x) =
  bind
    (body (s := r) (MkWith x))
    (\v -> bind (release x) (\c -> pure (closedWith v c)))

-- | The thing `acquire` gives, held by `body` in a region of its own --
-- | it is not kept past it -- and released by `release` when `body`
-- | ends: what it came to, or why the thing was not acquired or not
-- | released.  Should `body` be left otherwise -- a throw heard outside
-- | it, a handler between that drops the continuation -- the thing is
-- | let go of where the program drops its last reference to it, as its
-- | provider says.
scoped : {e : HFunctor}
       -> {err r a : Type}
       -> Co e (Either err r)
       -> (r -> Co e (Either err Unit))
       -> ({s : Type} -> With s r -> Co e a)
       -> Co e (Either err a)
scoped acquire release body = bind acquire (heldBy release body)
